WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.931
Your slide deck already explains something well.

2
00:00:03.981 --> 00:00:08.693
Here's how to make it work without you in the room, by turning it into a video.

3
00:00:09.193 --> 00:00:12.034
A deck on its own relies on a presenter.

4
00:00:12.084 --> 00:00:19.083
A video carries the slides and the explanation, so anyone can watch whenever suits them, and everyone hears the same message.

5
00:00:19.593 --> 00:00:28.519
You have three ways to convert: export from PowerPoint, record your screen, or use a dedicated converter that builds the video from your notes.

6
00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:30.479
Tidy the deck first.

7
00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:37.586
Keep one idea per slide, make each headline the point, and move detail into the speaker notes, where it becomes narration.

8
00:00:38.836 --> 00:00:40.609
Your speaker notes are your script.

9
00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:43.570
Write spoken sentences, not reminders.

10
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.811
They run longer, but they're much easier to follow by ear.

11
00:00:48.061 --> 00:00:51.842
Upload your deck, pick a voice, and download the MP4.

12
00:00:51.892 --> 00:00:53.862
Try Basic first.

13
00:00:53.912 --> 00:00:57.020
On Pro, AI directs an animated explainer.

14
00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.576
Visit powerpoint2vid.com.

